    dcterms:title                 "Linked.Archi ArchiMate 3.2 Derivation Rules"@en ;
    dcterms:description                '''SHACL rules (sh:SPARQLRule) implementing the ArchiMate 3.2 derivation
rules of Appendix B: DR1–DR8, whose derived relationships are valid in any model, and PDR1–PDR12,
whose derived relationships may hold. Each rule is the join its definition states; the restrictions of
B.4 and the order of strength are written into each rule. A
valid rule derives a statement: the direct triple, the qualified predicate and the resource, a
relationship like any other. A potential rule derives a proposition: the resource alone, which reifies
the triple (rdf:reifies) without asserting it, for the modeller to confirm by asserting the triple, with
its qualified predicate. Either way the resource carries its certainty (:Valid or :Potential),
the relationships it was derived from (prov:wasDerivedFrom) — the qualified relationships the rule
matched, the modeller's or derived — and the activity that generated it (prov:wasGeneratedBy): the
derivation activity, the rule applied to them, whose plan is the rule (prov:qualifiedAssociation,
prov:hadPlan). Each rule is a prov:Plan. What runs the rules — an application, a pipeline — records
its run: an activity of its own, with its agent and when it ran, of which each derivation activity it
produced is part (dcterms:isPartOf). What the modeller stated is told from what a rule derived by the
graph, in a store (a derivation is kept in .../graph/derived), and by the resource. Before the rules run,
:QualifyRelationships gives each relationship the model states only as a direct triple a resource of
its own. The IRIs are in the
model's namespace, a derivation's and its derivation activity's from its rule and premises; with no model
loaded, or several, in urn:linked-archi:. The rules are SPARQL 1.2. A rule
derives only from relationships whose triple is asserted, in the model or by a valid derivation
— one that is only :Potential is for the modeller to confirm, as is any other proposition — so the rules give the closure of valid
derivations and one layer of potential ones; a valid derivation of a relationship that so far is only
:Potential makes it :Valid. A potential rule derives only what the relationship tables of Appendix B.5
permit between the two element types, as archimate3.2-relationship-tables.ttl gives them: load it with
the model.
Generated from Appendix B (inline style).'''@en ;
